    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0508" n="412" xml:id="pg412"/>

                <head>No. 304.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 30, 1872</date>.
                        (Received April 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 538.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 536, I have
                    the honor to inclose herewith a copy and translation (A and B) of the reply of
                    Mr. Mariscal to my note of the 20th instant relative to the frequency of murders
                    by Mexicans in Arizona. This reply, though dated the 23d instant, was not
                    received until several days later.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d304-a1.xml" xpointer="d304-a1"/>
            </div>
